        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "People have always moved from one place to another throughout history. The idea that crossing an imaginary line makes someone illegal is something we reject completely. Borders are artificial constructs created by states to control people. No human being is illegal. The real problem is not people seeking better lives but the systems that label them as criminals for simply existing in a different location. When we remove these artificial barriers we also remove the tools that allow exploitation of vulnerable workers. Freedom of movement is a basic human right and no government should have the power to decide where a person is allowed to live."
        },
